course: dictionary
lesson: 12166
title: Compote: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Compote» is one of these words. Read the words around it first and ask what fits.
explain: «We spooned warm apple compote over our porridge.» Porridge and warm apple tell you compote is fruit cooked until soft, served as a dessert or with breakfast food. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Grandma poured us a glass of sweet compote from the big jar.» A glass and a poured drink show that compote can be a drink. In families from Ukraine and Eastern Europe, compote is a common homemade drink children have with dinner.
fact: Compote is a noun: one compote, two compotes.
fact: «Compote» means fruit cooked slowly with sugar and a little water until soft.
fact: In Ukraine, Russia and Poland, «compote» can mean a sweet drink made by boiling fruit or berries in water with sugar.
fact: «Compote» can also mean a bowl on a stem for serving fruit or sweets, but this meaning is rare.
fact: Phrases you may meet: «apple compote», «berry compote», «rhubarb compote», «a jar of compote».
exercise: «We spooned warm apple compote over our porridge.» What is the compote? | A bowl on a stem | *Fruit cooked slowly with sugar and water until soft | A cold drink from a glass bottle | A metal spoon
exercise: «In Ukraine, Grandma made a jar of compote to keep for the winter.» What kind of compote is most likely? | A kind of pasta | *A sweet drink made by boiling fruit in water with sugar | A bowl used for fishing | Hot soup with vegetables
exercise: Which phrase uses compote in the way a cook would? | Fish and chips | Chocolate cake | Sausage roll | *Berry compote
test: Compote is a noun. Which word is the plural of compote? | Compote's | *Compotes | Compotee
test: «The children ate rhubarb compote with yoghurt.» What does compote mean here? | *Fruit cooked with sugar until soft, served as a dessert | A pair of spoons | A grey, wet day | A bowl on a stem for fruit
exam: «Grandad poured us a glass of sweet compote from the big jar in the cellar.» What does compote mean here? | A bowl on a stem | Fresh raw fruit | A sort of pancake | *A sweet drink made by boiling fruit in water with sugar
